            <td height="6"> 
              <div align="center"><font size="4" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><b><font size="6">Re-occupation 
                of Palestinian land is no mere "retaliation"</font></b></font></div>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr align="left" valign="top"> 
            <td height="6"> 
              <hr>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr align="left" valign="top"> 
            <td height="298"> 
              <p> 
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3"> 
                <b>PMWATCH</b> -- June 19, 2002 -- Only those who choose to ignore 
                very recent and not so recent history, who elect to trump common 
                sense, who insist on turning their eyes away from the obvious, 
                can pretend that the decision by the government of Israel to re-occupy 
                Palestinian land was a mere "reaction", a "retaliation", 
                a "response" -- to use the favorite words of AP and 
                other news outlets here in the United States -- and was motivated 
                only by a desire to stop violence.</font></p>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">To begin with, 
                if indeed the intent of Ariel Sharon's violent policies against 
                Palestinians -- from assassination to land confiscation, to shelling 
                civilian areas, to flattening refugee camps -- has been to stem 
                violence against Israeli civilians, as he claims, one can only 
                characterize the results of this policy as nothing short of a 
                total disaster: since Mr. Sharon took office, in March 2001, 65 
                suicide bombings have hit Israel -- causing 238 Israeli deaths. 
                (<a href="http://story.news.yahoo.com/news?tmpl=story&amp;u=/ap/20020618/ap_wo_en_ge/israel_attacks_glance_3%20" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">read 
                more &gt;&gt;&gt;</a>) -- compared to ZERO deaths under Barak 
                between the time he took office and September 28, 2000 (and 5 
                deaths between September, 2000, and the time he left office, with 
                the first Israeli death from a suicide bombing taking place on 
                March 1, 2001).</font></p>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3">The 
                real reason why Mr. Sharon insists on dealing with Palestinians 
                only through violence and desruction can be easily gleaned if 
                only one were to bother and check the plentiful record. Indeed, 
                "Sharon is Sharon is Sharon", as an <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/manager/features/display_message.asp">April 
                13, 2001 Haaretz article</a> spelled out to those willing to look 
                at reality full face. </font><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3">Here 
                is an informative excerpt from that article: </font></p>
              <blockquote> 
                <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3">Sharon 
                  is the same Sharon and for him the War of Independence hasn't 
                  yet ended. In a comprehensive interview, <i><b>the prime minister 
                  describes the main points of his plan: Jerusalem, the Jordan 
                  Rift Valley and the Golan Heights are ours. Not even one of 
                  the settlements will be evacuated because they all have strategic 
                  and Zionist value. It is impossible at this time to bring about 
                  the end of the conflict, nor is separation from the Palestinians 
                  a viable concept. What then? Time is on our side</b></i>. (April 
                  13, 2001) <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/manager/features/display_message.asp">read 
                  more &gt;&gt;</a></font></p>
              </blockquote>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">So, let the 
                media know that their reporters may choose to write about Israeli 
                actions as if they were mere reactions rather than part of a fully 
                conscious game plan to keep Palestinian lands under Israeli control, 
                but that the rest of us who keep track of history know that Israel 
                is not, and never is, merely reacting out of "self-defense".</font></p>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">For more insight 
                on the broader context, read the <a href="#reinhart">article below</a> 
                by Prof. Tanya Reinhart from Tel Aviv University.</font></p>
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3">Palestine 
                Media Watch -- <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/index.html" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">http://www.pmwatch.org</a> 
                -- (610) 993 - 0608</font></p>
            </td>
          </tr>
